Now p9: drawGameWorld, draw dispatch, handlers, loop, init, debug API, closing.

Need to patch p6 for charge update and flash decay. Let me note:

In updateGame serving branch:
```js
if(G.charging){ G.charge=clamp((now-G.chargeStart)/700,0,1); }
```
Should be before using G.charge in position. Currently b.y uses G.charge; charge never updates. Add.

Also bumper flash decay: add near timers:
```js
for(const bm of bumpers) bm.flash=Math.max(0,bm.flash-0.06);
```
Add.

Also hitZombie/collectPowerup etc. Good.

Now p9:

```js
function drawGameWorld(){
  if(playBgCache) ctx.drawImage(playBgCache,0,0,W,H);
  drawPlayfieldFx();
  drawWalls();
  drawDecals();
  ctx.save();
  if(G.shake>0){ ctx.translate(rand(-G.shake,G.shake)*0.6, rand(-G.shake,G.shake)*0.6); }
  powerups...
  bumpers...
  zombies...
  flippers...
  balls...
  drawParticles();
  drawPops();
  ctx.restore();
}
```

Order: powerups behind zombies? Powerups should be visible; draw before zombies. Ball above all. Particles top. Fine.

`drawGame()`:
```js
drawGameWorld();
drawHUD();
drawBanner();
if(G.slow<1){ overlay cyan tint alpha 0.04 at playfield; }
```
The slow factor stored in G.slow by updateGame. Initially undefined; guard.

`draw()` dispatch with DPR transform:
```js
ctx.setTransform(DPR,0,0,DPR,0,0);
ctx.clearRect(0,0,W,H)? fill bg.
switch state...
```
Add `ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled=true`.

`update(step)`:
```js
G.t += step/1000;
if(G.state==='play') updateGame(step);
```

Input handlers:
- roles map.
- handleDown logic as designed. Need menu buttons.
- Mute button rect in all states? In game HUD yes. In overlays, mute still accessible? BTN.mute at top, overlays cover; let it work.
- Dog bark hitbox: menu states only; `if(G.state==='menu' && x>50&&x<325&&y>455&&y<600)`.
- Difficulty cards: select and store; play click; maybe update immediately. Keep menu open.
- Back buttons via BTN.back.
- Ranking back.
- Gameover again/toMenu.
- Play: if serving and y>H*0.5 → charging; else flippers; allow charge area entire bottom half (not top).
- For flippers while ball not serving: any x; if x<W/2 L else R.
- Also if a ball is serving but player taps top, nothing.
- Role management:
```js
const roles=new Map();
function handleDown(x,y,id){
 if(inRect(BTN.mute,x,y)){ toggleMute(); SFX.click(); return; }
 if(G.state==='menu'){...}
 ...
 if(G.state==='play'){
   if(G.chargingOrServing...)...
 }
}
```
Important: the mute button in play; but on gameover/difficulty/ranking, BTN.mute is visually not drawn except menu/playHUD? drawMuteButton is drawn in menu and HUD. In overlays, drawDifficulty/Ranking/GameOver call drawCredits but not mute; so mute rect shouldn't respond there. Check mute only in menu/play.

`handleUp` launch uses charge: `launchBall(0.35+0.65*G.charge)`. But `launchBall` takes power 0..1 and maps to velocity. Good.

Set G.charging false always; G.charge remains but irrelevant. Reset charge to 0 after launch in launchBall.

`startGame` should clear roles (release flippers): iterate and set hold false. Add `releaseFlippers()`.

State transitions:
- Menu start: startGame().
- Gameover again: startGame().
- toMenu: G.state='menu'; G.banner=''; G.toast=''; G.serving=false; maybe release.
- Ranking/diff back: G.state='menu'.

`initAssets`:
```js
titleCache=makeCache(W,118,buildTitle);
menuBgCache=makeCache(W,H,buildMenuBg);
playBgCache=makeCache(W,H,buildPlayBg);
initDust();
```

`loop` and start:
```js
let last=performance.now(), acc=0;
function frame(now){...}
requestAnimationFrame(frame);
```
Also handle visibility change: reset last when visible to avoid jump.
```js
document.addEventListener('visibilitychange',()=>{last=performance.now();acc=0;});
```

Debug API:
```js
window.WUMMI={...}
```

Initialize: initAssets(); initDust(); G.state='menu'; G.best=...; start loop.

Need to make sure `drawMenu` uses menuBgCache built. Yes.

Now also need to patch p6 after writing p9. Let me write p9.

One concern: `drawWummi` in menu called with opt.menu true for blink. In drawMenuBackground condition includes menu/diff/rank. Good.

Dog bark hitbox and drawBark both use G.barkUntil.

Also `G.barkUntil` set using performance.now().

`tagline` and buttons positions might overlap title cache (title y=56+118=174; subtitle at 201). Fine.

